# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:The Tourist Trap" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py; hand fixes: editor notes dropped, {{trandom}} options -> "Random Dialogue N" conds, Irena's skill menus -> the "Choose a reward skill" action, a "continues" splits the slave's lockpick and fail conds.
0	section	Starting off
1	box	Irena seems to be very upset and cries as you approach her.
1	line	Irena	Boo hoo! Oh dear, my only daughter....
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What's the matter?
2	line	Player	What's the matter?
2	line	Irena	Oh dear... my daughter, Ana, has gone missing in the desert. I fear that she is lost, or perhaps... *sob* even worse.
2	line	Player	When did she go into the desert?
2	line	Irena	*Sob* she went in there just a few days ago, *Sob* she said she would be back yesterday.
2	line	Irena	*Sob* And she's not...
2	select	Start The Tourist Trap quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	I'll find her for you!
3	line	Irena	Oh thank you! You've made me a very happy mother, I just hope it's not too late!
3	line	Player	Do you have any ideas on where she may have gone?
3	line	Irena	I did go looking for her myself and I came across some footprints just a little way south. I'm worried that they lead to the desert mining camp!
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	Oh... Well I hope you find her.
3	action	end
1	option	Cheer up, it might never happen.
2	line	Player	Cheer up, it might never happen.
2	line	Irena	It may already have happened you thoughtless oaf! My daughter, Ana, has gone missing in the desert. I fear that she is lost, or perhaps... *sob* even worse.
2	line	Player	When did she go into the desert?
2	line	Irena	*Sob* she went in there just a few days ago, *Sob* she said she would be back yesterday.
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Irena again
1	line	Irena	Please bring my daughter back to me. She is most likely lost in the Desert somewhere. I miss her so much... Wahhhhh! *Sob*
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Do you know where Ana went?
2	line	Player	Do you know where Ana went?
2	line	Irena	I did look for her myself and a little way south. I came across some footprints which may be hers. I'm worried that she may have been caught by some guards and taken to work in that terrible desert mine to the south.
2	action	previous
1	option	Is there anywhere around here that she would go?
2	line	Player	Is there anywhere around here that she would go?
2	line	Irena	I think she may have just gone a little way into the desert. It's unlike her to go too far away. She is an adventurous girl, but she knows how I worry. She wouldn't go too far.
2	action	previous
1	option	Where do you think I should start my search?
2	line	Player	Where do you think I should start my search?
2	line	Irena	I think I saw some of her footprints to the south, you could start there. Hopefully she'll just be over a few sand dunes, but you never know. She may have been taken to that awful desert mining camp or captured by
2	line	Irena	brigands!
2	action	previous
1	option	Okay, thanks.
2	line	Player	Okay, thanks.
2	action	end
0	section	Looking at the footprints
1	cond	Before starting the quest:
2	box	You see some footsteps in the sand.
2	action	end
1	cond	During the quest:
2	box	This looks like some disturbed sand. Footsteps seem to be heading off towards the South.
2	action	end
0	section	Searching the footprints
1	cond	Before starting the quest:
2	box	You see some footsteps in the sand.
2	action	end
1	cond	During the quest:
2	box	You search the footsteps more closely. You can see that there are five sets of footprints. One set of footprints seems lighter than the others. The four other footsteps were made by heavier people with boots.
2	action	end
0	section	Inspecting a cactus with a scarf on it
1	box	You remember that Irena mentioned something about Ana wearing a red scarf before she left for the desert.
1	action	end
0	section	Getting into the camp
0	section	Talking to a Mercenary
1	line	Mercenary	Yeah, what do you want?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What is this place?
2	line	Player	What is this place?
2	line	Mercenary	It's none of your business now get lost.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Perhaps five gold coins will make it my business?
3	line	Player	Perhaps five gold coins will make it my business?
3	cond	If the player does not have 5 coins:
4	line	Mercenary	Don't try to fool me, you don't have five gold coins! Before you try to bribe someone, make sure you have the money effendi!
4	line	Mercenary	Guards!! Guards!
4	line	Mercenary	Let's see how good you are with Desert Survival techniques.
4	box	You're bundled into the back of a cart and blindfolded...
4	action	The player is teleported somewhere north-west of the mining camp
4	box	Sometime later you wake up in the desert.
4	cond	If the player has any filled waterskins:
5	line	Guard	You won't be needing that water anymore!
4	box	The guards move off leaving you stranded in the desert.
4	action	end
3	line	Mercenary	Well, it certainly will help... -- The guard takes the five gold coins. -- Now then, what did you want to know?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	What is this place?
4	line	Player	What is this place?
4	line	Mercenary	It's just a mining camp. Prisoners are sent here from Al Kharid. They serve out their sentence by mining. Most prisoners will end their days here, surrounded by desert.
4	line	Player	So you could almost say that they got their ... 'Just Desserts'
4	line	Mercenary	You could say that... -- There is an awkward pause --
4	line	Mercenary	But it wouldn't be very funny.
4	line	Player	When they talk about 'the silence of the desert', this must be what they mean.
4	select	Select an Option
4	option	Can I take a look around the place?
5	line	Player	Can I take a look around the place?
5	line	Mercenary	Not really. The Captain won't let you in the compound. He's the only one who has the key to the gate. And if you talk to him, he'll probably just order us to kill you. Unless...
5	select	Select an Option
5	option	Does the Captain order you to kill a lot of people?
6	action	below
5	option	Unless what?
6	line	Player	Unless what?
6	line	Mercenary	Unless he has a use for you. He's been trying to track down someone called 'Al Zaba Bhasim'. You could offer to catch him and that might put you in his good books?
6	select	Select an Option
6	option	Where would I find this Al Zaba Bhasim?
7	line	Player	Where would I find this Al Zaba Bhasim?
7	line	Mercenary	Well, he could be anywhere. He's a nomadic desert dweller. However, they say that he's frequently to be found to the west in the hospitality of the tenti's.
7	select	Select an Option
7	option	The Tenti's, who are they?
8	line	Player	The Tenti's, who are they?
8	line	Mercenary	Well, we're not really sure what their proper name is. But they live in tents so we call them the 'Tenti's'.
8	select	Select an Option
8	option	Okay, thanks.
9	action	below
8	option	Is Al Zaba Bhasim very tough?
9	line	Player	Is Al Zaba Bhasim very tough?
9	line	Mercenary	Well, I'm not sure, but by all accounts, he is a slippery fellow. The Captain has been trying to capture him for years. A bit of a waste of time if you ask me. Anyway, I have to get going, I do have work to do.
9	action	end
7	option	Okay, thanks.
8	action	below
6	option	Okay, thanks.
7	action	below
4	option	Okay, thanks.
5	action	below
3	option	What are you guarding?
4	line	Player	What are you guarding?
4	line	Mercenary	Well, if you have to know, we're making sure that no prisoners get out. -- The guard gives you a disapproving look. -- And to make sure that unauthorised people don't get in.
4	line	Mercenary	-- The guard looks around nervously. -- You'd better go soon before the Captain orders us to kill you.
4	select	Select an Option
4	option	Does the Captain order you to kill a lot of people?
5	line	Player	Does the Captain order you to kill a lot of people?
5	line	Mercenary	-- The guard snorts. -- *Snort* Just about anyone who talks to him.
5	line	Mercenary	Unless he has a use for you, he'll probably just order us to kill you. And it's such a horrible job cleaning up the mess afterwards.
5	select	Select an Option
5	option	Not to mention the senseless waste of human life.
6	line	Player	Not to mention the senseless waste of human life.
6	line	Mercenary	Huh? Them's your words, not mine.
6	select	Select an Option
6	option	It doesn't sound as if you respect your Captain much.
7	line	Player	It doesn't sound as if you respect your Captain much.
7	box	-- The guard looks around conspiratorially. --
7	line	Mercenary	Well, to be honest. We think he's not exactly as brave as he makes out. But we have to follow his orders. If someone called him a coward, or managed to trick him into a one-on-one duel many of us bet that he'd be
7	line	Mercenary	beaten.
7	line	Player	And how could I trick him into a one-on-one duel?
7	line	Mercenary	Like all cowards, he likes to be made to feel important. If anyone insults him outright, he just gets us to do his dirty work. However, if he thinks he's better than you, if you compliment him, he may feel that he can defeat
7	line	Mercenary	you. And if he initiated a duel, all the men agreed that they wouldn't intervene. We think he'd be slaughtered in double quick time.
7	select	Select an Option
7	option	Can I have a bet on that?
8	line	Player	Can I have a bet on that?
8	cond	If the player already placed a bet:
9	line	Mercenary	Sorry, we've already taken your bet, wouldn't want any cheating now. Anyway, I have to get back to work. See ya around...
9	action	end
8	line	Mercenary	Well, if you think you stand a chance, sure. But remember, if he gives us an order, we have to obey.
8	select	Select an Option
8	option	I'll bet 5 gold that I win.
9	line	Player	I'll bet 5 gold that I win.
9	cond	If the player doesn't have enough gold:
10	line	Mercenary	Huh! It looks like you're betting with money you don't have.
10	action	end
9	line	Mercenary	Great, I'll take that bet.
9	box	You hand over 5 gold coins.
9	line	Mercenary	Ok, if you win, you'll get 6 gold back. Anyway, I have to get going, I do have work to do. -- The guard walks off. --
9	action	end
8	option	I'll bet 10 gold that I win.
9	line	Player	I'll bet 10 gold that I win.
9	cond	If the player doesn't have enough gold:
10	line	Mercenary	Huh! It looks like you're betting with money you don't have.
10	action	end
9	line	Mercenary	Great, I'll take that bet.
9	box	You hand over 10 gold coins.
9	line	Mercenary	Ok, if you win, you'll get 12 gold back. Anyway, I have to get going, I do have work to do. -- The guard walks off. --
9	action	end
8	option	I'll bet 15 gold that I win.
9	line	Player	I'll bet 15 gold that I win.
9	cond	If the player doesn't have enough gold:
10	line	Mercenary	Huh! It looks like you're betting with money you don't have.
10	action	end
9	line	Mercenary	Great, I'll take that bet.
9	box	You hand over 15 gold coins.
9	line	Mercenary	Ok, if you win, you'll get 19 gold back. Anyway, I have to get going, I do have work to do. -- The guard walks off. --
9	action	end
8	option	I'll bet 20 gold that I win.
9	line	Player	I'll bet 20 gold that I win.
9	cond	If the player doesn't have enough gold:
10	line	Mercenary	Huh! It looks like you're betting with money you don't have.
10	action	end
9	line	Mercenary	Great, I'll take that bet.
9	box	You hand over 20 gold coins.
9	line	Mercenary	Okay, if you win, you'll get 30 gold back. Anyway, I have to get going, I do have work to do. -- The guard walks off. --
9	action	end
