0	section	Talking to the Mercenary Captain
1	box	You approach the Mercenary Captain.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Wow! A real captain!
2	line	Player	Wow! A real captain!
2	line	Mercenary Captain	Be off effendi, you are not wanted around here.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	That's rude, I ought to teach you some manners.
3	line	Player	That's rude, I ought to teach you some manners.
3	line	Mercenary Captain	Oh yes! How might you do that? You seem little more than a gutter dweller. How could you teach me manners?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	With my right fist and a good deal of force.
4	line	Player	With my right fist and a good deal of force.
4	line	Mercenary Captain	Oh yes, ready your weapon then! I'm sure you won't mind if my men join in? Har, har, har! Guards, kill this gutter dwelling slime.
4	action	(Continues with Guards eviction dialogue.)
3	option	Err, sorry, I thought I was talking to someone else.
4	line	Player	Err, sorry, I thought I was talking to someone else.
4	line	Mercenary Captain	Well, Effendi, you do need to be careful of what you say to people. Or they may take it the wrong way. Thankfully, I'm very understanding. I'll just let my guards deal with you.
4	line	Mercenary Captain	Guards, teach this desert weed some manners.
4	action	(Continues with Guards eviction dialogue.)
2	option	I'd love to work for a tough guy like you!
3	line	Player	I'd love to work for a tough guy like you!
3	line	Mercenary Captain	Hmmm, oh yes, what can you do?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	I can mine!
4	line	Player	I can mine!
4	line	Mercenary Captain	Ha, ha, ha! You come to a mining camp and offer us your mining skills! Thanks effendi, but we have all the miners we'll ever need.
4	line	Mercenary Captain	Now be off with you, before we reduce you to a bloody mess on the sand.
4	select	Select an Option
4	option	Can't I do something for a strong Captain like you?
5	action	below
4	option	You don't scare me!
5	action	below
3	option	Can't I do something for a strong Captain like you?
4	line	Player	Can't I do something for a strong Captain like you?
4	box	The Captain ponders a moment and then looks at you critically.
4	line	Mercenary Captain	You could bring me the head of Al Zaba Bhasim.
4	line	Mercenary Captain	He is the leader of the notorius desert bandits, they plague us daily. You should find them west of here. You should have no problem in finishing them all of. Do this for me and maybe I will consider helping you.
4	select	Select an Option
4	option	Consider it done.
5	line	Player	Consider it done.
5	line	Mercenary Captain	Good... run along then. You stand around flapping your tongue chatting like an insane camel.
5	action	end
4	option	Sorry Sir, I don't think I can do that.
5	line	Player	Sorry Sir, I don't think I can do that.
5	line	Mercenary Captain	Hmm, well yes, I did consider that you might not be right for the job. Be off with you then before I turn my men loose on you.
5	select	Select an Option
5	option	It's a funny captain who can't fight his own battles!
6	line	Player	It's a funny captain who can't fight his own battles!
6	box	The men around you fall silent and the Captain silently fumes. All eyes turn to the Captain...
6	line	Mercenary Captain	Very well, if you're challenging me, let's get on with it!
6	box	The guards gather around to watch the fight.
6	action	(The Mercenary Captain attacks.)
5	option	Okay, I'll be moving along then.
6	line	Player	Okay, I'll be moving along then.
6	line	Mercenary Captain	Effendi, I think you'll find that is the wisest decision you have made today.
6	action	end
1	option	You there!
2	line	Player	You there!
2	line	Mercenary Captain	How dare you talk to me like that! Explain your business quickly... or my guards will slay you where you stand.
2	box	Some guards close in around you.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	I'm lost, can you help me?
3	line	Player	I'm lost, can you help me?
3	box	The captain smiles broadly and with a sickening voice says...
3	line	Mercenary Captain	We are not a charity effendi, Be off with you before I have your head removed from your body.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	What are you guarding?
4	action	below
3	option	You don't scare me!
4	line	Player	You don't scare me!
4	line	Mercenary Captain	Well, perhaps I can try a little harder. Guards, kill this infidel.
4	action	(Continues with Guards eviction dialogue.)
2	option	What are you guarding?
3	line	Player	What are you guarding?
3	line	Mercenary Captain	Effendi...
3	line	Mercenary Captain	For just one second, imagine that it's none of your business!
3	line	Mercenary Captain	Also imagine having your limbs pulled from your body one at a time.
3	line	Mercenary Captain	Now, what was the question again?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Do you have sand in your ears? I said, 'What are you guarding?'
4	line	Player	Do you have sand in your ears, I said, 'What are you guarding?'
4	line	Mercenary Captain	Why... you ignorant, rude and eternally damned infidel, -- The Captain is very angry at what you just said. -- Guards, kill this infidel!
